different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,999 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the presence of multiple awardees do not indicate improper conduct. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for repeated purchases and verify if multiple contracts served the same purpose. Review awardee A's contracts to ensure no single supplier was overused for similar needs.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["q%2F46T6hnq1K7JOCXkOhcDg%3D%3D","SFcMgX9zyIBJ8Trn0ZPzLw%3D%3D","hHR5DRFp6XXE6P%2FuLemXRw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}